From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:53:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: rockchip-vpu: add the RK3588 AVS+ decoder
 registers

The VPU121 of the RK3588 has an AVS+ (GY/T 257.1) decoder next to it, at
0xfdb51000. It has the register layout of a Hantro G1 decoder and shares
the interrupt line, clocks, power domain, resets and IOMMU of the VPU121
decoder. The vendor kernel describes it as a separate device that shares
the task queue and reset group of the VPU121, so the hardware is never
used by both at the same time.

Describe it as a second, optional register range of the VPU121 node,
named "avsd", rather than as a node of its own: the driver then runs it
as one more function of that device, in the same job queue. The RK3328
has the same block at 0xff351000, next to its VPU.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/media/rockchip-vpu.yaml          | 24 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip-vpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip-vpu.yaml
index 8c2501634080..4ab9e340ac76 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip-vpu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip-vpu.yaml
@@ -37,7 +37,16 @@ properties:
           - const: rockchip,rk3568-vpu
 
   reg:
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: VPU registers
+      - description: AVS+ decoder registers
+
+  reg-names:
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - const: vpu
+      - const: avsd
 
   interrupts:
     minItems: 1
@@ -87,6 +96,19 @@ required:
   - clocks
   - clock-names
 
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      not:
+        properties:
+          compatible:
+            contains:
+              const: rockchip,rk3588-vpu121
+    then:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          maxItems: 1
+        reg-names: false
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
